      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>The destination delivery handover for a two‑wheeler or motorcycle is the final verification stage that confirms the vehicle arrives in the same condition as it left the origin, and that all mileage records are accurate before ownership is transferred.</p>

<h3>Daylight Condition Re‑inspection</h3>
<p>Upon arrival the vehicle is examined in natural daylight to eliminate shadows that could hide surface damage. The inspector compares the live view with the original pickup photographs, noting any new scratches, dents, paint chips, or missing accessories.</p>
